        "original_id": "4d165d73-a21e-5c45-af90-70afea9a9f47",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Sparaxis, Campanula, Dierama pendulum\n- Families: Iridaceae, Campanulaceae\n- Places: Cape Province, South Africa\n- Concepts: genus classification, taxonomic reclassification\n\nFacts:\n- Sparaxis, also called harlequin flower, is a genus in the family Iridaceae.\n- Sparaxis includes about 13 species endemic to Cape Province, South Africa.\n- Campanula is one of several genera in the family Campanulaceae with the common name bellflower.\n- Before its current classification, Dierama pendulum had been placed in various genera including Ixia, Sparaxis, and Watsonia.",
